 "notes": [
  "The last statement of a session idle in a transaction needs Performance Schema (events_statements_current), which MariaDB ships off (and its events_statements_current consumer is off by default even with Performance Schema on).",
  "The oldest open transaction (connection 79, 20 min 52 s) runs under REPEATABLE READ, so after its first consistent read it keeps a read view until it ends: InnoDB cannot purge the undo logs that view may still need, and the history list length grows.",
  "Statuses are rules of thumb, not verdicts. The summary counts every session this account can see; the filters narrow only the list. This tool's own session is left out."
 ],
